( '119', '15', '7', 'Stores store information and Models are probably templates.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '120', '15', '8', 'Events happen when people click things.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '121', '16', '1', 'let allows the value to change, const does not allow reassignment, and var is an older declaration with different scoping rules.', '4.00', NULL, 'You mentioned differences in reassignment and scoping but lacked details on redeclaration and specific use cases for each declaration type.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '122', '16', '2', 'async and await allow code to handle operations that complete later. For example, the application may wait for an HTTP response.', '6.00', NULL, 'Good understanding of async and await, but lacked an explicit explanation of how they work with Promises. The example is relevant but could be expanded for clarity.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '123', '16', '3', 'Arrays are good for lists and objects are good for information with named fields.', '6.00', NULL, 'You correctly pointed out the basic uses of objects and arrays, but your answer was too vague and missed detailed differentiation and specific examples of when to use each.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '124', '16', '4', 'Scope means which parts of the program can access a variable. Global, function and block scopes have progressively smaller visibility.', '7.00', NULL, 'You clearly defined variable scope and identified the three major types effectively, but the differences were too general without examples for context.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '125', '16', '5', 'A component is a reusable Ext JS UI element. Examples include grids, forms, panels, fields and windows.', '8.00', NULL, 'Well done identifying components and providing examples. However, more detail on their configuration and how they interact in an application would strengthen your answer.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '126', '16', '6', 'A DataGrid displays records in tabular form. Usually the Store provides the records and the columns map fields to what the user sees.', '7.00', NULL, 'You captured the essence of the DataGrid, but your answer could use more depth regarding how data flows and its relationship with the Store.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '127', '16', '7', 'Models define individual records and Stores manage sets of those records.', '5.00', NULL, 'You made a correct distinction between Models and Stores but did not elaborate on how they work together. More detail on the relationship would improve your response.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '128', '16', '8', 'Events are used to react to user activity. You can register handlers for button clicks or grid row selection.', '7.00', NULL, 'You articulated the role of events well, but your examples could be more specific to demonstrate a deeper understanding of handling events.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '129', '17', '1', 'var is function scoped, subject to hoisting behavior and permits redeclaration. let and const are block scoped and are inaccessible in the temporal dead zone before initialization. let permits reassignment while const does not permit reassignment of the binding.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '130', '17', '2', 'An async function always returns a Promise. await performs asynchronous suspension of that function until a Promise settles, allowing other event-loop work to proceed. It is useful for I/O-bound operations such as HTTP requests.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '131', '17', '3', 'Arrays are specialized objects with ordered integer-indexed elements and array methods. Ordinary objects associate named property keys with values. Selection depends on whether the data conceptually represents a sequence or a keyed structure.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '132', '17', '4', 'JavaScript uses lexical scoping. Global scope contains top-level bindings, function scope applies notably to var declarations, and block scope applies to let, const and class declarations within blocks.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '133', '17', '5', 'Ext JS components are instances of the framework UI component hierarchy, providing configuration, lifecycle, rendering, layout participation and event handling. Applications compose them into nested container trees.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '134', '17', '6', 'The DataGrid renders tabular views of Store records. A Store manages Model instances, while column configurations define field mapping, rendering, sorting and other presentation behavior.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '135', '17', '7', 'Models define record schemas, conversions, validation and potentially associations or proxy behavior. Stores manage collections of records and support loading, synchronization, sorting, grouping and filtering.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '136', '17', '8', 'The Ext JS observable/event architecture allows components and stores to publish named events. Listeners, controllers and ViewControllers can bind handlers to those events and respond to user or data changes.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '137', '18', '1', 'const is for something you do not plan to reassign, let is for something you might reassign, and var is the older style with function scope.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '138', '18', '2', 'async and await make asynchronous code easier to read. await can be used when waiting for data from an API.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '139', '18', '3', 'An array represents a list and an object represents something with named properties.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '140', '18', '4', 'Scope is where a variable can be seen. Global is widest, then function, then block.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '141', '18', '5', 'Ext JS has components like buttons, grids, forms and windows. They are combined to build the application UI.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '142', '18', '6', 'The DataGrid displays Store records in rows and configured fields in columns.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '143', '18', '7', 'A Model is one kind of record definition, while a Store manages multiple records.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '144', '18', '8', 'Components fire events and listeners respond to them.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '145', '19', '1', 'var belongs to function scope. let and const belong to block scope. const forbids reassignment, while let permits it.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '146', '19', '2', 'An async function returns a Promise, and await suspends that function until the Promise resolves or rejects.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '147', '19', '3', 'Arrays preserve an ordered collection of values. Objects organize values by property keys.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '148', '19', '4', 'Scope is lexical visibility. A binding may live globally, within a function, or within a block.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '149', '19', '5', 'An Ext JS component is a configurable UI object participating in rendering, layout and events. Examples include Grid, Panel, Window, Button and Form fields.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '150', '19', '6', 'The grid renders rows from Store records and columns from field-oriented column definitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '151', '19', '7', 'Models describe records; Stores aggregate and manage them.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '152', '19', '8', 'Events provide notifications of actions or state changes. A listener executes when the corresponding event fires.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '153', '20', '1', 'let and const are block scoped. var is usually function scoped. const means the variable cannot be reassigned, but the contents of an object can still change.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '154', '20', '2', 'async and await help handle Promises and server requests without writing long callback chains.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '155', '20', '3', 'Arrays are lists with ordered positions. Objects use names for each value.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '156', '20', '4', 'Global scope is outside functions. Function scope is inside one function. Block scope is inside braces such as if or for blocks.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '157', '20', '5', 'A component is a building block for an Ext JS interface, like a grid, panel or form.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '158', '20', '6', 'The grid displays rows from records in a Store. Columns decide which fields are visible.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '159', '20', '7', 'Models define fields and Stores contain records based on those Models.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '160', '20', '8', 'You can listen for events such as click, change, or grid selection and run a handler when they occur.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '161', '21', '18', 'Weather describes short-term atmospheric conditions at a particular place and time, such as rain today or a temperature of 30 degrees. Climate describes the typical weather patterns of a region over many years. For example, a storm tomorrow is weather, while a desert having generally dry conditions is climate.', '8.00', NULL, 'Good distinction between weather and climate but the examples could be more specific. The term \'storm tomorrow\' could confuse as it\'s not a typical case of weather.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '162', '21', '19', 'Large cities often develop near rivers and coastlines because water provides transportation, trade routes, drinking water, food, irrigation, and access to ports. Historically, moving goods by water was also much easier than transporting them over land.', '9.00', NULL, 'Well detailed explanation of the benefits of water proximity to cities, including historical context.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '163', '21', '20', 'Water heats and cools more slowly than land. Oceans therefore reduce temperature extremes near the coast by absorbing heat during warmer periods and releasing stored heat during cooler periods.', '9.00', NULL, 'Good explanation of how water affects temperature moderation in coastal areas.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '164', '21', '21', 'A time zone is a geographic region that follows the same standard clock time. Time zones are necessary because Earth rotates, so different parts of the planet experience daylight at different times.', '10.00', NULL, 'Clear and accurate definition of time zones with a solid connection to Earth\'s rotation.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '165', '21', '22', 'A continent is a major geographic landmass, such as South America. A country is a political territory with its own government, such as Brazil. A city is an urban settlement inside a country, such as Rio de Janeiro.', '9.00', NULL, 'Clearly defined each term with examples, but could clarify the order of definitions for smoother understanding.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '166', '21', '23', 'Mountains affect climate because temperature normally decreases with elevation. They can also force moist air upward, causing rain on one side of the mountain and creating a drier rain-shadow region on the opposite side.', '10.00', NULL, 'Excellent explanation of how mountains influence climate.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '167', '21', '24', 'A desert is defined mainly by having very little precipitation, not by temperature. Some deserts are extremely hot, while others are cold. Polar regions can even be classified as deserts because they receive little precipitation.', '10.00', NULL, 'Great distinction regarding the definition of deserts focusing on precipitation.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '168', '21', '25', 'Geography can influence an economy through natural resources and transportation. A country with oil or minerals may develop industries around those resources, while access to navigable rivers and ocean ports can make international trade easier and less expensive.', '9.00', NULL, 'Identified key geographic influences effectively but could improve by elaborating on natural resources’ impact on economic sectors.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '169', '21', '26', 'Population density is the number of people living in a given area, often measured as people per square kilometer. Two countries can have the same population but very different densities if one country has a much larger land area.', '9.00', NULL, 'Good definition of population density, but the second part could be a little clearer.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '170', '21', '27', 'Fertile farmland can support agriculture and food production. Rivers provide water, irrigation, transportation, and potentially hydroelectric power. Ocean access allows ports, fishing, shipping, and international trade. Together these features can encourage economic and population growth.', '10.00', NULL, 'Excellent overview of the benefits of geographic features mentioned in the question.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '176', '22', '18', 'Weather is what the atmosphere is doing now or over a short period, while climate describes the normal weather of an area over many years. Rain this afternoon is weather and a tropical region being warm most of the year is climate.', '8.00', NULL, 'Good explanation of the difference between weather and climate, but the example of climate could be more specific.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '177', '22', '19', 'Water helped cities grow because people needed drinking water and because rivers and oceans made transportation and trade easier.', '7.00', NULL, 'You mentioned key reasons for city growth near water but could have expanded on historical contexts.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '178', '22', '20', 'The ocean changes temperature more slowly than land, so it helps keep nearby places from becoming extremely hot or extremely cold.', '9.00', NULL, 'Clear explanation of how temperature regulation by water affects coastal areas.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '179', '22', '21', 'A time zone is an area where people use the same time. We have different zones because different parts of Earth receive sunlight at different times as Earth rotates.', '10.00', NULL, 'Excellent definition and explanation of time zones relative to Earth\'s rotation.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '180', '22', '22', 'A continent is a large land region like Europe. A country is a nation such as France. A city is a populated place within a country, such as Paris.', '9.00', NULL, 'Well done in distinguishing country, continent, and city with valid examples.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '181', '22', '23', 'Mountains are colder at higher elevations and they can affect rainfall because clouds may release rain as air moves over the mountains.', '8.00', NULL, 'Good explanation of elevation effects but could clarify the rain shadow effect more.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '182', '22', '24', 'Deserts are places with very little rain. They do not necessarily have to be hot because some deserts can be cold.', '10.00', NULL, 'Good definition of deserts focusing on precipitation rather than temperature.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '183', '22', '25', 'A country near an ocean can benefit from shipping and international trade. A country with fertile land can also produce more agricultural products.', '9.00', NULL, 'Good explanation of benefits related to geographic features to the economy.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '184', '22', '26', 'Population density measures how many people live in an area. A small country with 10 million people would usually be more densely populated than a very large country with the same population.', '8.00', NULL, 'Defined population density well but could clarify population distribution more.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '185', '22', '27', 'The farmland would help grow food, rivers could provide water and transportation, and the ocean would allow trade with other countries.', '10.00', NULL, 'Excellent explanation of the benefits of geographic features.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '191', '23', '18', 'Weather changes from day to day and climate is the general weather of a place. A rainy day is weather and a generally hot region describes climate.', '6.00', NULL, 'Your answer identifies that weather changes day to day and gives an example, but it lacks depth in distinguishing between short-term and long-term patterns effectively.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '192', '23', '19', 'Cities near water have easier access to water and transportation.', '5.00', NULL, 'You mentioned access to water and transportation but did not explain other relevant factors that support cities, such as trade and historical settlement.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '193', '23', '20', 'The ocean prevents temperatures near the coast from changing as quickly because water takes longer to heat up.', '8.00', NULL, 'Good explanation of the moderating effect of water on temperatures, but could expand on the cooling and warming processes to gain full credit.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '194', '23', '21', 'A time zone is an area using the same clock. They exist because it is daytime in some parts of Earth while it is nighttime in others.', '8.00', NULL, 'You\'ve defined time zones and related them to day and night, which is clear. However, more detail on Earth\'s rotation would enhance your response.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '195', '23', '22', 'North America is a continent, Canada is a country, and Toronto is a city.', '10.00', NULL, 'Excellent job clearly distinguishing country, continent, and city, along with appropriate examples for each.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '196', '23', '23', 'Mountains are usually colder at the top and can also cause some places near them to receive more rain.', '6.00', NULL, 'Your answer touches on temperature differences, but does not fully explain the rain shadow effect or elevation\'s role in climate variation.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '197', '23', '24', 'A desert is an area that does not receive much rain, so deserts can also be cold.', '10.00', NULL, 'Excellent explanation of what defines a desert with emphasis on precipitation, clearly addressing the key criteria.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '198', '23', '25', 'Natural resources can help a country make money and being close to the ocean can make trade easier.', '8.00', NULL, 'You\'ve identified natural resources and proximity to the ocean as factors; more details on how these factors specifically influence the economy would enhance your response.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '199', '23', '26', 'Population density is basically how crowded a country is. A smaller country can be more crowded even when another country has the same number of people.', '7.00', NULL, 'Your explanation of population density is solid, but you could enhance it by discussing land area or distribution differences more explicitly.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '200', '23', '27', 'The farmland can be used to grow food and the rivers provide water. Ocean access helps ships enter and leave the country.', '6.00', NULL, 'You mentioned some benefits of each feature, but further elaboration on how they specifically benefit economic development would strengthen your answer.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '206', '24', '18', 'Weather is rain, snow, heat and things happening outside. Climate is usually what a place is like.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '207', '24', '19', 'People like living near the water and boats can travel there.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '208', '24', '20', 'The ocean makes coastal places cooler because there is a lot of water nearby.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '209', '24', '21', 'Time zones are different times used in different countries.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '210', '24', '22', 'Africa is a continent, Egypt is a country and Cairo is a city.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '211', '24', '23', 'Mountains can be cold and sometimes have snow.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '212', '24', '24', 'Deserts usually do not have much water. Some can be cold.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '213', '24', '25', 'Countries with beaches can make money from tourists.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '214', '24', '26', 'Population density means how many people live somewhere.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '215', '24', '27', 'They could grow crops and use boats in the ocean.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '221', '25', '18', 'Weather and climate are basically the same thing.', '0.00', NULL, 'Your response did not address the differences between weather and climate.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '222', '25', '19', 'Most large cities are near water because people like beaches.', '2.00', NULL, 'You mentioned that many cities are near water, but the reasoning lacks depth and clarity.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '223', '25', '20', 'Coastal areas are always warmer because oceans are hot.', '2.00', NULL, 'Your answer suggested that coastal areas are warmer without explaining temperature regulation.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '224', '25', '21', 'A time zone is the amount of time it takes to travel somewhere.', '1.00', NULL, 'Your definition of a time zone was not accurate and did not relate to Earth\'s rotation.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '225', '25', '22', 'Mexico is a continent, America is a country and Texas is a city.', '1.00', NULL, 'Your examples confused the categories of country, continent, and city.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '226', '25', '23', 'Mountains make every nearby place colder.', '2.00', NULL, 'Your answer oversimplified the impact of mountains on temperature.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '227', '25', '24', 'A desert is any place that is extremely hot.', '2.00', NULL, 'You identified extreme heat but did not mention precipitation as the defining factor.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '228', '25', '25', 'Geography does not really affect an economy because businesses can operate anywhere.', '0.00', NULL, 'Your response fails to recognize the influence of geography on economics.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '229', '25', '26', 'Population density is the total population of a country.', '1.00', NULL, 'Your definition of population density was incomplete.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '230', '25', '27', 'The country would have nice scenery and places for tourists.', '2.00', NULL, 'Your answer identified a benefit but did not elaborate on economic implications.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '236', '26', '28', 'In a solid, particles are closely packed and mainly vibrate in fixed positions, so solids have a fixed shape and volume. In liquids, particles remain close but can move past each other, so liquids keep their volume but take the shape of the container. Gas particles move freely and spread out, so gases have neither fixed shape nor fixed volume.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '237', '26', '29', 'Heating gives the liquid particles more kinetic energy, so they move faster. Eventually some particles have enough energy to overcome attractive forces in the liquid and enter the gas phase.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '238', '26', '30', 'Plants use sunlight as the energy source for photosynthesis. They use light energy along with carbon dioxide and water to produce sugars, storing energy chemically, and oxygen is released.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '239', '26', '31', 'Gravity is an attractive force between masses. Earth has a large mass, so its gravity pulls objects toward its center. This produces weight and causes unsupported objects to fall.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '240', '26', '32', 'Mass describes the amount of matter in an object and remains essentially constant. Weight is the force of gravity acting on that mass, so an object can weigh differently on Earth and the Moon even though its mass remains the same.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '241', '26', '33', 'Ice is less dense than liquid water. When water freezes, hydrogen bonding creates an open molecular structure that places the water molecules farther apart, decreasing its density.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '242', '26', '34', 'Renewable energy comes from sources that are replenished naturally on a human timescale, such as solar energy. Nonrenewable resources are finite or take extremely long periods to form, such as coal.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '243', '26', '35', 'Bacteria are important decomposers. They break down dead organisms and waste, returning nutrients to ecosystems where those nutrients can be reused by plants and other organisms.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '244', '26', '36', 'Repeating experiments helps scientists determine whether results are reproducible rather than accidental. Repetition also helps reveal random errors and increases confidence in a conclusion.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '245', '26', '37', 'Both spoons can be at the same room temperature. Metal has much higher thermal conductivity than wood, so it transfers heat away from the hand faster. The rapid loss of heat from the skin makes the metal feel colder.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '251', '27', '28', 'Solid particles stay closely packed and only move slightly, so a solid keeps its shape. Liquid particles can move around one another and take the shape of the container. Gas particles are far apart and move freely.', '8.00', NULL, 'Good description of particle movement and state behaviors, but missed the explicit mention of volume for liquids and gases.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '252', '27', '29', 'The particles absorb energy when heated and move faster until they can separate from the liquid and become gas.', '10.00', NULL, 'Well explained the process of heating and particle separation. Great job!', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '253', '27', '30', 'Sunlight provides energy for photosynthesis. Plants use the energy to make sugar from water and carbon dioxide and release oxygen.', '10.00', NULL, 'Excellent explanation of the role of sunlight in photosynthesis and the production of sugars.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '254', '27', '31', 'Gravity is the force that attracts objects with mass. Earth\'s gravity pulls objects downward toward the planet.', '9.00', NULL, 'Good definition of gravity and its effect on objects; could benefit from mentioning weight explicitly.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '255', '27', '32', 'Mass is the amount of matter in something. Weight depends on gravity, so your weight could change on another planet but your mass would stay the same.', '10.00', NULL, 'Clear distinction between mass and weight, well done!', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '256', '27', '33', 'Ice floats because ice has a lower density than liquid water.', '8.00', NULL, 'Correctly stated that ice has a lower density; more detail on molecular structure would strengthen the answer.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '257', '27', '34', 'Renewable energy can naturally be replaced, such as solar or wind. Nonrenewable energy is limited, like oil or coal.', '9.00', NULL, 'Good job defining renewable and nonrenewable energy with examples!', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '258', '27', '35', 'Some bacteria help humans digest food and some help decompose organic material in nature.', '9.00', NULL, 'Great examples of bacterial roles; mentioning other diverse roles could enhance the response.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '259', '27', '36', 'Repeating experiments allows scientists to make sure the result happens consistently and was not just an accident.', '9.00', NULL, 'Well articulated the importance of repeating experiments for consistency.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '260', '27', '37', 'Metal transfers heat better than wood. Heat moves from your hand into the metal more quickly, so the metal feels colder even if both spoons started at the same temperature.', '10.00', NULL, 'Excellent explanation of thermal conductivity differences between materials!', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'evaluated', NULL, NULL ),
( '266', '28', '28', 'Solids keep their shape because their particles do not move around much. Liquids move more and take the shape of their container. Gas particles move freely and fill the available space.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '267', '28', '29', 'The particles move faster when they are heated. If enough heat is added, the liquid becomes a gas.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '268', '28', '30', 'Plants need sunlight to make their food through photosynthesis. They use sunlight, water and carbon dioxide.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '269', '28', '31', 'Gravity is the force that pulls things toward Earth and keeps us on the ground.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '270', '28', '32', 'Mass is how much matter an object contains. Weight is how strongly gravity pulls on it.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '271', '28', '33', 'Ice floats because it is less dense than water.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '272', '28', '34', 'Solar power is renewable because sunlight continues to be available. Oil is nonrenewable because there is only a limited supply.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '273', '28', '35', 'Some bacteria help the digestive system and others can cause diseases.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '274', '28', '36', 'Scientists repeat experiments to see if they get the same answer again.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '275', '28', '37', 'Metal conducts heat quickly, so when you touch it the heat in your hand moves into the spoon faster than it does with wood.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '281', '29', '28', 'A solid is hard, a liquid is wet and a gas is usually invisible. Their particles move differently.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '282', '29', '29', 'When a liquid gets hot enough it evaporates and the particles begin moving around more.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '283', '29', '30', 'Plants need sunlight so they can grow and produce food.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '284', '29', '31', 'Gravity pulls objects downward and stops us from floating away.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '285', '29', '32', 'Mass is how heavy something is and weight is the number shown on a scale.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '286', '29', '33', 'Ice is lighter than water so it stays on the top.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
( '287', '29', '34', 'Renewable energy does not run out quickly. Solar energy is renewable and gasoline is nonrenewable.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL ),
